paragraph(intro,'Established methods are referenced',r"Established methods are referenced where introduced. The coordinate transforms, geometric heuristics and combined selection criteria are design choices developed for this system. The numerical substitutions below use the configured mechanism, stored handwriting and recorded offline processing traces; their inputs and scope are collected in Appendix~\ref{app:des-real-calculations}. They establish how the calculations operate, while physical performance is assessed separately in Results. Occasional module pointers identify implementation detail in the separately submitted source.")

# Mechanical calculations use known geometry/settings. Unknown physical measurements cannot be invented.
paragraph(hw,'Motor torque must be assessed',r'Motor torque must be assessed at operating speed, rather than from holding torque alone. The generated Owen job uses a travel feed of 2400\,mm/min and drawing feed of 900\,mm/min. With the installed 40\,mm/revolution transmission, these correspond to 60 and 22.5\,rev/min respectively, using Equation~\ref{eq:des-rpm}.')
p=B/hw;s=p.read_text().replace(r'\frac{4000}{40}=100',r'\frac{2400}{40}=60');p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
paragraph(hw,'Calculated example: For a chosen acceleration case,','')
paragraph(hw,'At constant speed, only the resistance term remains.',r'At constant speed, Equation~\ref{eq:des-torque} reduces to $T=r_pF_f=0.006366F_f$\,N\,m for the installed pulley, with $F_f$ in newtons. A numerical load margin requires measured carriage resistance, moving mass and reflected inertia. The available record does not establish these quantities sufficiently to substitute a verified operating load. The driver starts each segment without a controlled acceleration ramp, so a holding-torque rating alone cannot establish an allowable starting rate.')
m=r['motion_segment']
paragraph(hw,'Algorithm~\\ref{alg:des-stepping} gives the major-axis form',rf"Algorithm~\ref{{alg:des-stepping}} gives the major-axis form of the implemented loop. In the generated Owen file, the segment from $(17.024,239.996)$ to $(17.065,239.643)$\,mm produces signed count changes $(3,-29)$ at the configured nominal 80 microsteps/mm. For example, the $x$ increment is $\operatorname{{round}}(17.065\times80)-\operatorname{{round}}(17.024\times80)=1365-1362=3$. The $y$ axis is therefore the major axis, with initial accumulator $\lfloor29/2\rfloor=14$; the three $x$ pulses are distributed among the 29 $y$ pulses. This evaluates the generated command at the nominal scale, rather than assuming a recovered physical homing count.")
paragraph(hw,'Calculated example: For an illustrative 10 mm move',r'For that same generated segment, $d=\sqrt{0.041^2+0.353^2}=0.355373$\,mm, $v=900/60=15$\,mm/s, $N_M=29$ and $N_m=3$. Equation~\ref{eq:des-pulsetime} gives $\tau=0.355373/(15\times29)=0.000816950$\,s and $t_{\rm delay}=32\tau=0.0261424$\,s. The geometric feed budget is $d/v=0.0236915$\,s. The extra delay follows from the separate minor-axis pulses; neither value is a measured motor execution time.')
paragraph(hw,'Calculated example: Using the configured',r'The configured travel dimensions give usable spans $200.6-2(5)=190.6$\,mm and $261.3-2(5)=251.3$\,mm after edge clearance. These values define the generated job\textquotesingle s workspace. The numerical calibrated values of $\kappa_x$ and $\kappa_y$ additionally require the actual switch-to-switch counts $N_x,N_y$; a count has not been substituted where its measurement is unavailable.')
paragraph(hw,'For example, allocating 0.25',r'At the configured maximum $x$ travel, the multiplier in Equation~\ref{eq:des-scaleerror} is $190.6/200.6=0.95015$. Thus reference-length uncertainty contributes approximately $0.95015|\delta L_x|$ at the far end of the usable axis. This converts the actual geometry into a sensitivity coefficient; a measured uncertainty still requires the travel measurement and switch-repeatability record.')
paragraph(hw,'Here $R_S$ is the carrier',r'Here $R_S$ is the carrier\textquotesingle s sense resistance and $V_{\mathrm{ref}}$ is the measured reference voltage. The installed motor\textquotesingle s 1.68\,A phase rating gives the conditional electrical bound $V_{\rm ref}\leq8R_S(1.68)$. If the reported R10 marking is confirmed as $R_S=0.10\,\Omega$, this is $V_{\rm ref}\leq1.344$\,V before considering a lower limit imposed by carrier heating. This is a component-rating constraint, not the recorded adjustment: the actual current setting cannot be calculated without a measured $V_{\rm ref}$.')
paragraph(hw,'The reported resistor marking is tentatively',r'The reported resistor marking is tentatively R10 and must be checked before applying that bound. The ODROID uses its supplied mains adapter; its DC output rating remains to be confirmed separately from the 24\,V stepper supply. The dedicated ODROID 3.3\,V rail supplies the installed 3.3\,V loads, including the pen motor. The GPIO connections carry the associated control and feedback signals.')

paragraph(seg,'Calculated example: With illustrative',r'In the Owen01 page trace, pixel $(y,x)=(317,343)$ of the $800\times600$ pre-deskew working image has $G=100$. Its 41 by 41 background window gives $B_r=161.43367$, hence $R=100/161.43367=0.619449$. The selected ratio threshold is $0.803906$, so this pixel enters the ink mask. These values come from the actual photograph after the documented reduction, rather than chosen grey levels.')
paragraph(seg,'Calculated example: For four prefix entries',r'The same pixel\textquotesingle s four prefix values are $20696850$, $18404173$, $18359673$ and $16338366$. Equation~\ref{eq:des-integral} gives a window sum of $271370$, so $B_r=271370/1681=161.43367$. This is the local-background value used in the preceding mask decision.')
paragraph(seg,'Calculated example: For a constructed candidate',r'For this page\textquotesingle s ratio histogram, the selected bin is 171. Its masses are $\omega_0=0.07069375$ and $\omega_1=0.92930625$, with mean bin indices 124.98356 and 217.71913. Their between-class variance is approximately $564.97942$ in squared bin-index units. Converting the selected bin centre to the ratio scale gives $t^*=(171+0.5)(1.2/256)=0.80390625$, the threshold used above.')
paragraph(seg,'Calculated example: Two candidate row profiles',r'The Owen01 angle search gave squared-projection scores of 442973 at $+0.5^\circ$, 464105 at $+1.0^\circ$ and 439403 at $+1.5^\circ$. The maximum over all seventeen tested angles was 464105, so the routine selected $+1.0^\circ$. These scores are computed from the reduced mask used by the angle search, before the final mask is rebuilt.')
ss=r['seam'];sc=r['seam_cost']
paragraph(seg,'Calculated example: For local cost',rf"In the traced boundary between centres 38 and 61, the selected predecessor at column 283 changes from row 50 to row 49 in working-image coordinates. Its stored predecessor cost is $0.00641966$, the movement penalty is $0.02$ and the new local cost is $0.0000226843$. Equation~\ref{{eq:des-seam}} therefore gives $D\simeq0.00641966+0.02+0.0000226843=0.02644234$. This traces one selected minimum of the actual dynamic programme; equal-cost alternatives can also occur.")
paragraph(seg,'Calculated example: With $h_g',r'At that boundary point, $y_m=(38+61)/2=49.5$, $h_g=(61-38)/2=11.5$ and the closed mask is zero. The implemented local cost is therefore $C=0.012[(49-49.5)/11.5]^2=0.0000226843$. It provides the local term used in the preceding accumulated-cost calculation.')
paragraph(seg,'Calculated example: A chosen',r'The archived first Owen01 line is $156\times2170$ pixels. Its fit scale is $a=\min(64/156,640/2170)=0.2949309$, giving a $46\times640$ resized image after integer rounding. The routine places it nine rows below the top of the 64-row canvas, retaining its aspect ratio and filling the remaining rows with white.')

paragraph(net,'Calculated example: In one illustrative',r'For the first Owen01 line, channel 0 of the first convolution at canvas row 34, column 462 gives $\sum WX=-1.150897$ with learned bias $b=-0.000435125$. Equation~\ref{eq:des-conv} therefore produces $z=-1.151332$. The nine actual input and learned-weight values are retained in Appendix~\ref{app:des-real-calculations}; this is a traced activation, not a chosen filter.')
paragraph(net,'Calculated example: For illustrative',r'At the same activation, the checkpoint stores $\mu=0.2163021$, $\sigma^2=0.02585394$, $\gamma=1.0193636$ and $\beta=0.1324657$. Using $\epsilon=10^{-5}$ in Equation~\ref{eq:des-bn} gives $y=1.0193636(-1.1513321-0.2163021)/\sqrt{0.02585394+10^{-5}}+0.1324657\simeq-8.53619$. The following ReLU sets this negative response to zero. These are the stored inference statistics, rather than statistics calculated from this single line.')
paragraph(net,'Calculated example: One scalar cell',r'In the first forward LSTM layer for that line, frame 10 and cell 0 have $c_{t-1}=-2.7277257$, $f_t=0.7306111$, $i_t=0.6666368$ and $g_t=-0.8560218$. Equation~\ref{eq:des-lstm} gives $c_t\simeq-2.5635625$. With $o_t=0.000145395$, the cell emits $h_t\simeq-0.000143680$. This records the memory calculation used while processing the real feature sequence.')
paragraph(net,'Calculated example: For a two-frame',r'For the complete labelled line ``1.9. Vloggers using fame to support charities is a positive way'', the recorded forward--backward total is $\log Z=-0.47033843$. Equation~\ref{eq:des-ctc} gives $\mathcal L_{\rm CTC}=0.47033843$ and $Z\simeq0.6247908$. This loss was evaluated offline from the trained reader\textquotesingle s actual logits and known transcript, without updating its weights.')
paragraph(net,'Calculated example: In that example,',r'At frame 11, the probability of \texttt{V} is $p_{11,V}=0.98030665$ and the target-constrained occupancy is $q_{11,V}=0.99999995$. The CTC logit derivative is therefore $p-q=-0.01969329$. It is negative because the admissible target paths require more \texttt{V} probability than the current output supplies at that frame; the real-input finite-difference check in Appendix~\ref{app:des-expanded-checks} checks this derivative.')
paragraph(net,'For the illustrative transcript',r'The word ``Vloggers'' in this actual transcript contains adjacent \texttt{g}s. They require separate emission runs with a blank between them: a direct skip between identical label states would collapse to one character. The same restriction is retained during forced alignment in Section~\ref{sec:des-alignment}; training sums admissible paths, whereas extraction selects one.')
paragraph(net,'Calculated example: At the selected',r'The same Owen crop has an estimated body-band height of 38 pixels. At the selected $\rho=0.17$, the width calculation gives $w=\operatorname{clip}(\operatorname{round}(0.17\times38),2,9)=6$, then $k=2\lfloor6/2\rfloor+1=7$. The actual redraw therefore uses a seven-pixel square dilation before fitting the line to the network canvas.')
