paragraph(rep,'Calculated example: If $p_t',r'For the \texttt{V} in that Owen line, frame 11 corresponds to state 11 of the blank-interleaved transcript. Its log emission is $-0.01988991$ and the three admissible predecessor scores are $-13.91888$, $-10.01139$ and $-1.3624485$. Equation~\ref{eq:des-viterbi} selects their maximum and gives $V=-0.01988991-1.3624485=-1.3823384$. Backtracking assigns \texttt{V} the frame interval $[11,12)$.')
paragraph(rep,'Calculated example: For illustrative smoothed',r'The refined right boundary of this \texttt{V} is source column 193. Although smoothing gives $\overline p_{193}=2.8$ and the positive-column reference is 14.36, the raw ink count at column 193 is zero. The explicit blank-column rule therefore overrides $2.8/14.36$ and assigns zero cut cost. This is a real case in which the gap rule prevents smoothing alone from penalising a clean separation.')
paragraph(rep,'Calculated example: With chosen',r'A traced point on this \texttt{V} is $(x,y)=(173,59)$, with left cut $x_L=146$, baseline $b=107$, $h_x=38$ and $\tan\phi=-0.0787017$. Equation~\ref{eq:des-glyphcoords} gives $v=48/38=1.263158$ and $u_0=27/38-1.263158(-0.0787017)=0.809939$. After the implementation\textquotesingle s three-decimal intermediate rounding and measured post-trim shift $\delta=0.4472489$, the stored point is $(u,v)=(0.363,1.263)$ and the recorded lead is 0.447 x-heights.')
paragraph(rep,'For unit-length descriptor',r'For unit-length descriptor $v_g$ and the normalised median reference $r_c$ for character $c$, the prior distance is $d(g,c)=1-v_g^Tr_c$. Internal consensus instead uses pairwise $L_1$ descriptor distances and chooses the medoid with the lowest total distance. These compare a pooled character reference with this writer\textquotesingle s own forms. Dylan\textquotesingle s first stored \texttt{a} variant has recorded prior distance 0.114. Recomputing the pairwise rule on all nine final stored variants gives the smallest total distance, 33.3413, for variant index 4; the other totals range from 34.4306 to 42.9091. This demonstrates the selection rule on the final pool, without treating a new descriptor calculation as the historical filtering log. Algorithm~\ref{alg:des-profile} gives its place in profile construction.')
paragraph(rep,'Calculated example: If twelve',r'For the single extracted Owen line used above, 39 eligible adjacent non-space glyph pairs were counted and three boundaries were crossed by a recovered skeleton. Equation~\ref{eq:des-connectedness} gives $c=3/39=0.076923$. This line-level extraction trace illustrates what is counted; the final stored writer profile summarises its own complete source collection.')
pl=r['placement']
paragraph(rep,'Calculated example: Using the preceding',rf"In the generated Owen sentence ``Writing with style.'', the first placement call uses $(u,v)=({pl['u']:.8f},{pl['v']:.8f})$, lead $l={pl['lead']:.8f}$, zero shear and drift, and $h_x^{{\rm mm}}=4$. With the initial placement origin $(0,0)$, Equation~\ref{{eq:des-placement}} gives $x=4({pl['lead']:.8f}{pl['u']:+.8f})={pl['x']:.7f}$\,mm and $y=4({pl['v']:.8f})={pl['y']:.7f}$\,mm. This is the actual assembly point before later path processing and machine placement, not a replay of the earlier \texttt{{V}} crop.")
paragraph(rep,'Calculated example: An illustrative median',r'The final Owen profile\textquotesingle s stored glyph distances have median $\widetilde d=0.18355$. Equation~\ref{eq:des-anchor} gives $\lambda=\operatorname{clip}[(0.18355-0.24)/0.08,0,1]=0$. With no stored override, this is the anchoring value selected by the automatic rule for the generated job.')
