paragraph(rep,'Calculated example: For a 20-character',rf"For the recorded Owen candidate 1, the 19-character target ``Writing with style.'' differs from its reader output by one substitution, giving $A=18/19={ca['A']:.7f}$. The selected-writer posterior is $P={ca['P']:.7f}$, so Equation~\ref{{eq:des-jointscore}} gives $J={ca['J']:.7f}$. This is the actual score used to select the candidate in Figure~\ref{{fig:des-candidates}}; it evaluates the software rendering rather than physical stylistic agreement.")
paragraph(rep,'Here $t$ is intended text',r'Here $t$ is intended text, $\widehat t$ is recognised text, $d_{\mathrm{edit}}$ is the minimum number of insertions, deletions and substitutions, using the reader error convention~\cite[PDF p.~2, Sec.~2.1]{graves2006}, and $P$ is the model probability of the selected writer. The harmonic mean $J$ in Equation~\ref{eq:des-jointscore} makes a weak component limit the combined score. The actual candidate comparison below holds text and writer fixed, making the effect of the writer posterior visible without inventing scores.')
paragraph(rep,'Calculated example: For a chosen origin',r'The generated Owen trajectory has $x_0=0.9593369$\,mm and $y_1=6.6340616$\,mm. A point $(2.9829210,5.3303251)$\,mm is placed using the configured origin $(0,251.3)$\,mm, margins $(15,10)$\,mm, unit fit scale and zero line shift. Equation~\ref{eq:des-machinecoords} gives $(x_m,y_m)=(17.0235840,239.9962635)$\,mm. Three-decimal file emission writes this point as \texttt{X17.024 Y239.996}, connecting the trajectory calculation to the motion segment examined in Section~\ref{sec:des-drive}.')
paragraph(rep,'The physical x-height is first chosen',r'The physical x-height is first chosen from the page ruling and a stored x-height-to-pitch ratio where available. If that ratio is absent, the configured fallback gives $8.4(0.46)=3.864$\,mm at the default 8.4\,mm ruling. This is the fallback sizing rule, rather than the value passed to every job: the traced Owen job explicitly requests 4\,mm. A probe of the requested text can reduce the selected value if robust line extent exceeds 1.25 rulings. The extent uses the 98th-percentile stroke tops and second-percentile bottoms, with exact extremes for fewer than eight strokes. It limits outliers but does not guarantee every extreme lies inside the nominal band.')
paragraph(rep,'The generated file selects millimetres',r'The generated file selects millimetres and absolute positioning. A travel move reaches the start of a stroke with the pen raised, the pen is lowered, drawing moves follow, and the pen is raised before the next travel. Figure~\ref{fig:des-gcode-excerpt} reproduces the beginning of the actual generated Owen file used for these calculations. The interpreter assigns \texttt{M3} and \texttt{M5} to pen down and pen up respectively.')
